          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A library records whether visitors use the study area or borrow a book on a given visit. On a particular day, the probability a visitor does at least one of these activities is ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "0.85",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", and the probability a visitor borrows a book is ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "0.6",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p13-q36-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find the probability that a visitor uses the study area but does not borrow a book.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$0.25$",
      "worked": "Let $S$ be using the study area and $B$ be borrowing a book. The union consists of borrowing visitors and study-only visitors.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(S\\cap\\overline{B})&=P(S\\cup B)-P(B)\\\\P(S\\cap\\overline{B})&=0.85-0.6\\\\P(S\\cap\\overline{B})&=0.25\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
